# Independent production-site CI checker review

Final decision: no remaining blocking finding in this bounded CI/static-artifact/browser scope. Reviewed uncommitted .github/workflows/ci.yml and tools/audit/site/check.py,test_check.py against source2390e31127b4d8173c872f61abc48689a24c3cc4. Reviewer made no production edits; root implemented all corrections.

Initial findings were real and reproduced in repro.py/repro.json with browser stubs solely to isolate static validation: a build-only bundle returned passed with zero cases, stale/mixed source commits were accepted, and duplicate manifest records were accepted. Initial four rejection subcases passed but did not cover these cases. Root corrected the checker to require nonempty HTML, exact current-registry route coverage plus both indexes, current Git commit in both build/manifest, committed config/base, current design identity, docs-only/null runtime capability, original source digests, renderer executable identity and exact nonduplicate outer/nested manifest membership. Build manifest byte sizes are mandatory; Doc manifest has no byte-size fields in its existing schema, so its hashes remain the relevant checks.

Independently exercised corrected expected-input validation against the real primary bundle: positive identity passes; stale commit, wrong base, missing page, wrong source digest and wrong renderer reject. Executed final unit suite:3 tests pass, including15 rejecting subcases and a real temporary Git checkout positive fixture. Empty HTML and duplicate records now reject explicitly. Independently verified Python -O exits1 with the intentional assertions-required error. Simulated missing runner propagates failure instead of being skipped. The final complete static gates pass for both actual site-final-primary and site-final-alternate bundles before that simulated runner boundary.

Real browser execution by this reviewer: primary96 cases pass and alternate96 cases pass, Chromium/Firefox/WebKit x16 HTML pages x2 widths, JavaScript disabled. Primary ran the initial checker; alternate ran the corrected identity checker before the final design/capability/size checks. Final changes affect static gates only; the browser loop is unchanged, and those final static gates were independently exercised for both bundles as above. primary.json and alternate.json preserve actual case measurements and artifact identity. A first alternate invocation collided with the newly mandatory --renderer CLI flag and exited2; it was rerun with the correct renderer/config arguments, and the failed invocation is not a browser pass. Browsers verify200 responses, no failed/error responses, stylesheet presence and no horizontal overflow. Static code checks duplicate IDs and local file/fragment closure. This is not a new human visual/screen-reader or deployment claim.

CI uses the existing pinned Playwright installation and all three matching engines, generates fresh production bundles at both project bases and passes the actual target/debug/nepl3-tools executable plus alternate config to the checker. Quality already depends on doc-browser and requires its success; no publishing permission or dependency bypass was added. Runner/assertion/hash/link errors terminate the job. always artifact upload is limited to dist/doc-browser; include-hidden-files preserves .nojekyll. The job retains its20-minute outer deadline. Source/renderer identities are independently compared rather than trusting mutually consistent archive metadata alone. This tool is scoped to generated repository-site artifacts, not a universal untrusted HTML sanitizer or remote-authentication proof.

git diff --check passes. Root's workspace Rust tests, Clippy and repository checks are separately owned; they were not rerun by this reviewer. Actual GitHub final-head CI remains required before integration. reviewed-check.py, reviewed-test_check.py and reviewed-ci.yml bind the exact final files examined; earlier failures remain in separate evidence rather than being rewritten as success.
